SUMMARY:Little Bradley Falls\; a Challenge
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nWe are the HFF Trail Trekkers: We a’gonna
  get our step-counters a’workin’ !!\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v
 =Bsh_8qxUfDY**\nUp to 12 of you are welcome to join me.\n**THIS IS AN EXPL
 ORATORY EVENT.**\nDistance: 3.75 miles Total\; Initial descent: 300 ft\; t
 hen: Accum Ascent: 550 ft.\n3 ea wet creek Xings.\n**NOTE: STORM DAMAGED T
 RAIL:** Hazards may include: washed out sections\, landslides\, eroded are
 as\, muddy slippery footing\, and downed clusters of trees.\nPace: **1.5mp
 h – because I’m an ol’ Codger.**\nDifficulty: challenging **(READ FU
 LL DESCRIPTION BELOW)**\n**Masticating will be ‘in motion’.**\n**Optio
 nal: wading/swimming available.**\nWeather Check: Saluda\, NC.\nWeather ca
 ncellations will be posted at 6:30am.\nDrive time: 10 mi/1/4 hr 1-way\nApp
 rx return time: 2:30 pm\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN O
 N.\nI currently have 1.5 driver(s) (6ppl)\nCarpool contributions appreciat
 ed. $2.00 suggested\nWe suggest open windows while carpooling. Only you kn
 ow your own health status so judge accordingly if an event may endanger yo
 ur health or the health of others.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to
  avoid bringing your muddy shoes into the driver's car at the end of the h
 ike.\nIncessant prattlers will be assumed to be having an affair. My attem
 pts to quiet the prattlers has failed. This has become a ‘social network
 ing’ event.\n**THIS IS A DOG-PARTICIPANT HIKE.** This event is NOT for t
 hose who are uncomfortable with the antics of fun-loving dogs. Well traine
 d dogs **(you don’t have to yell)** can be 'off-leash'.\n**Dogs MUST enj
 oy DEEP water Xings!!!!**\nSmall (lap)dogs may carpool. Large dogs will dr
 ive themselves.\n**DESCRIPTION\;**\nRemember - hikes led by ‘the Curmudg
 eon’ tend to have challenging surprises. **Please don’t flick the fair
  flighty fairies…**\n**LITTLE BRADLEY FALLS.**\nTrail Condition: 1.25 mi
  (1-way) Accum ascent: 350 ft. Slope traverse\; roots\; some very short st
 eep sections\; One short narrow section of 6”wide rock traverse. **2 ea 
 KNEE-DEEP water Xings.** Watershoes\, change of heavy socks\, & towels ***
 NECESSARY***. Plastic bags for key fobs & phone suggested.\nStorm Damage: 
 3 landslide sections that we traverse.\nAll hikes are at your own risk. Yo
 u are responsible for your OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: The
  organizer of this event is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The 
 function of the organizer is only to organize this event. There are certai
 n risks inherent in any outdoor activity. Each participant\, by signing up
  to attend this event\, agrees to release from liability the leader(s)\, H
 endo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and members for any acciden
 t\, injury\, illness\, or personal loss which might occur while participat
 ing in this activity or while traveling in any vehicle during this trip. *
 *Each participant further agrees to abide by the rules and regulations con
 cerning safety\, to follow instructions of the leader(s)\, and not to beco
 me intentionally separated from the group.** The leader(s) also has the ri
 ght to use any images collected on this trip for recording on website phot
 o collections.\ngordie's contact: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(**before** d
 ay of hike): 828.393.0297 (talk & text)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/ph
 otos/146993931@N05/albums**
